        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            LVP and laminate are both good floors when they are in the right room. Vinyl's plastic core makes it the default wherever water shows up, and laminate's hard surface and wood-like feel make it the better value in the dry rooms where most of a house's floor area is.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Decide room by room rather than for the whole house, compare each material on its own rating scale, and respect the expansion gaps and underlayment rules. Do that and either floor will still look good years from now.
          </p>
